# Cloudflare's, for every file it serves of deploy/site/ (wrangler.jsonc):
# the wallet's build, which deploy/stage.js places at wallet/, writing this
# beside it as deploy/site/_headers. Cloudflare reads that and doesn't serve
# it. What no file answers, deploy/worker.js does, with the same but its own
# policy, as its answers are no pages.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is the one the build's pages carry (kit.csp,
# svelte.config.js, from scripts/csp.js), which stage.js puts in place of
# PAGE_POLICY: the wallet's own scripts alone, SvelteKit's inline ones by
# their hashes, WebAssembly, what the wallet reads from, and frame-ancestors,
# which a page's own policy can't say.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: PAGE_POLICY
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/wallet/_app/immutable/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
